<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Community News – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em; margin-top: 5px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Community News</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Reporting From the School!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: productive: Write personal journal entries about daily experiences. interactive: Write a short descriptive text about personal plans for various activities.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write personal journal entries describing recent community events they attended (e.g., 'Last weekend, I went to the Desfile de las Mil Polleras. I liked the colorful dresses and the music. It was really fun!'). Can write short descriptions of personal plans for upcoming community activities (e.g., 'Next month, I will visit Pedasi for Carnivals. I want to see the parade and the Carnival Queen's floats.'). Can create a simple community news report about a local event using descriptive adjectives (e.g., 'The school fair was last Friday. There were games, food stands, and music. Many students helped organize it, and everyone had fun.').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task (Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</b><br>
                Students activate prior knowledge and connect to the theme "Reporting From the School!"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various pictures of local school events from previous years (e.g., a school fair, a cultural event with traditional dances, a mural decoration project). Students work in pairs to brainstorm 3-5 words or short phrases to describe what they see in each picture, writing them down. The teacher encourages use of adjectives like <i>colorful, traditional, exciting</i>, and nouns like <i>fair, mural, festival</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher shows one picture of a school event and models writing a simple sentence about it using the past simple tense and an adjective. For example: "Last Friday, the students <b>decorated</b> a <b>colorful</b> banner for the <b>school fair</b>. It <b>was</b> very fun!" The teacher points to 'decorated' and 'was' and emphasizes the past tense. The teacher also models describing a person in the picture: "Look at the teacher. She <b>is tall</b> and has <b>curly hair</b>. She <b>was friendly</b> to everyone."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did this event happen now or in the past?" (Expected answer: In the past!)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What kind of words help us describe the event or people?" (Expected answer: Adjectives! Like colorful, friendly, tall.)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>
                Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Community News".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, simple community news report from the school, written on a handout or displayed on the board. The report describes a recent school event (e.g., "The School Sports Day").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example Text:</b><br>
                "<b>School Sports Day Success!</b><br>
                Last Friday, our school celebrated a fantastic Sports Day! Many students <b>participated</b> in different games like running and jumping. The weather <b>was sunny</b>, and everyone <b>felt excited</b>. The teachers <b>prepared</b> healthy snacks, but some students also brought delicious food. Mr. Carlos, our new P.E. teacher, <b>is tall</b> and has <b>black straight hair</b>; he helped organize everything. It was a wonderful cultural event for our school <b>community</b>."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Sharing past experiences and preferences, describing people and community members.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> The teacher reads the report aloud, highlighting key vocabulary (<i>celebrated, participated, prepared, community, excited, fantastic, tall, black straight hair</i>) and past simple verbs. Students then answer:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What event did the school celebrate?" (Gist)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"True or False: The students didn't participate in games." (True/False)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Who organized the event?" (Information question)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>
                Accuracy focus on Writing. Students practice target grammar and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences using past simple tense, compound sentences with 'but', and descriptive adjectives (physical appearance, feelings). Vocabulary: <i>community, celebrated, participated, prepared, excited, friendly, tall, curly hair, black eyes</i>, etc.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides a handout with incomplete sentences related to school events. Students complete them using the correct past simple form of verbs or appropriate adjectives from a word bank. (e.g., "Last month, our class ___ (decorate) a beautiful mural." "The Carnival Queen had ___ (long/short/curly) hair.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Combining):</b> The teacher gives two simple sentences and students combine them into one compound sentence using "but". (e.g., "The students liked the games. They didn't like the loud music." -> "The students liked the games, but they didn't like the loud music.") The teacher ensures students practice both 'liked' /t/ and 'didn't' /d/ sounds in their heads as they write. Students also write a sentence describing a community member from a picture, using adjectives for physical appearance (e.g., "Ms. Elena is short and has black eyes.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Guided Writing (Event Description):</b> Students are given a topic sentence like "Our school had a great cultural event last week." In pairs, they write 2-3 additional sentences, describing what happened using past simple verbs and adjectives. The teacher circulates, providing support and checking for correct usage. For example: "Our school had a great cultural event last week. Many families <b>gathered</b>. We <b>saw</b> traditional dances. The dancers <b>wore colorful Polleras</b>."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>
                Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Community News".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual writing task: Students write a short community news report or a journal entry about a recent school event (real or imagined). They should aim for 4-5 sentences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher reminds students of the model news report from Stage 2 and the practice activities from Stage 3.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students choose one of these prompts:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Write a short news report about our school's recent talent show."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Write a journal entry about a fun day you had at school last month."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students must include:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least three verbs in the past simple tense (e.g., <i>celebrated, went, liked, participated, prepared</i>).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two descriptive adjectives (e.g., <i>colorful, exciting, friendly, tall</i>).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One compound sentence using "but" if applicable (e.g., "I liked the music, but I didn't like the long speeches.").</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students write their report/entry on a piece of paper or in their notebooks. The teacher provides support and guidance as needed, reminding students to use vocabulary like <i>community, festival, fair, parade, cultural event</i> if appropriate.</li>
                </ol>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>
                Formative assessment of student learning and self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their written news reports/journal entries with a partner for peer assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer Checklist - Students check YES/NO):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did my partner use at least three past simple verbs correctly?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did my partner use at least two descriptive adjectives?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did my partner use "but" correctly in a sentence? (If applicable)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the report/entry clear and easy to understand?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">*Optional: Suggest one way to make the report even better (e.g., "I like your report, but maybe you could add more adjectives to describe the food.").</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students write their answers on a small slip of paper.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or grammar rule I used in my writing today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did I learn about writing about past school events?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b><br>
                Review of the lesson and connection to future learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing a news report was easy for me? What was difficult?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can writing about school events help my community?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The students successfully used the past simple tense and some descriptive adjectives in their reports. The sentence combining with "but" was a bit challenging for some, requiring more focused practice. Peer assessment fostered collaborative learning and awareness of criteria. Next time, I will provide more sentence frames for the 'but' structure and review past tense -ed endings quickly. The overall learning outcome for writing simple news reports was achieved.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will apply all the learned vocabulary and grammar to create a collaborative "Community News Bulletin Board" for the school, integrating their writing with visual elements and presenting their findings. This will consolidate their ability to report on community news.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>